Reference only (nothing copied)
  Adafruit Fruit Jam (CC BY-SA): the pin map, the hub, DDC and DAC wiring,
  and what its power path lacks were read from its design. No sheets,
  symbols, footprints or geometry are copied.

  Texas Instruments datasheets SLAS671C (TLV320DAC3100) and SLVSBC5D
  (TPD13S523): the source of the two symbols' pin tables, which
  tools/board/make_library.py draws.

  Raspberry Pi 3-pin Debug Connector Specification (RP-003139-SP): the SWD
  connector's pinout and its 100 ohm series resistors at the target.

  C&K PTS645 Series datasheet (B-136 to B-139, Apr 21): the holes of
  hardware/board/lib/liz4270.pretty/SW_CK_PTS645V_Angled.kicad_mod, a
  footprint of our own drawn from its PCB layout for termination V, with the
  frame's legs as pad SH. Its 3D model is KiCad's stock PTS645Vx39 body,
  named by path and not copied.

  IBM 3174/3274 Control Unit to Device Product Attachment Information
  (October 1986; bitsavers.org, pdf/ibm/3174/): section 1.4.5.4, feature 6
  (the 3180 Advanced Function feature) and its RDINFO request, from which
  tools/capture/rdinfo.py and the feature 6 notes in docs/upstream-review.md
  were written (#112). Facts about the protocol only; no text is copied.

  IBM 3270 Data Stream Programmer's Reference (GA23-0059-07, June 1992;
  bitsavers.org, pdf/ibm/3174/): the Usable Area and Alphanumeric Partitions
  query replies, by which tools/capture/rdinfo.py decodes UAQRV and PRTQRY
  (#112). Facts about the protocol only; no text is copied.

  IBM SNA Management Services Formats (GC31-8302-01, March 1998;
  bitsavers.org, pdf/ibm/sna/): the Hardware Product Identifier's fields and
  their character set, cited in docs/upstream-review.md for the plant code
  RDINFO carries (#112). Facts only; no text is copied.


