Run-time dependencies (not copied)
----------------------------------

tools/capture/ imports pycoax 0.11.2 and oec master (hanshuebner/oec-tcp)
at run time and copies no code from them. It reuses oec's serial read fix by
importing it (oec/__main__.py, _read_through_the_descriptor, written by Hans
Hübner in oec master), and the keymap cross-check imports oec's keymaps. Both
are ISC; the repository notice is "Copyright (c) 2019, Andrew Kay". The display code ranges in coaxlog.to_display (blank, digits, a-z, A-Z)
are facts about the 3483-V character set, as photographed in
coax-tcp/protocol/character-map.jpg.

tools/sim/ imports the same pycoax 0.11.2 and oec master at run time, and
sliplib 0.6.2 (MIT, "Copyright (c) 2015 Ruud de Jong"; pycoax already depends
on it). It copies no code from them. iface2.py answers oec as current
interface2 firmware does: the message format (length, payload and trailer;
RESET, the features query, and TRANSMIT_RECEIVE with its repeat count) is
implemented from what pycoax's serial_interface.py sends and what
coax-tcp interface2/firmware/src/interface.cpp answers, with no code taken
from either. The display code table in tools/sim/display_codes.py is
transcribed from our own photographs of the 3483-V
(captures/photos-20261003/); a test compares it with oec's CHAR_MAP
(oec/display.py) as a cross-check.
Its keymap tests and keymap_doc.py also feed the translator's output to oec's
Keyboard and keymap_ibm_typewriter (oec master
@ 3c5e812f6d2c0321e6c443dd4ed9590b7611c58a) as a cross-check; the scan codes
themselves come from the captures.

tools/sim/rig.py drives the bench through pyserial 3.5 (BSD-3-Clause,
Chris Liechti), as pycoax does, and copies no code from it.

The PNG renderer in tools/sim/screen.py imports Pillow (MIT-CMU, the SPDX
name for the historical PIL licence, as Pillow 12 declares it).
tools/sim/subset_font.py imports fontTools (MIT); it only rebuilds the font
subset and isn't needed to run anything.
tools/sim/bake_font.py imports fontTools and Pillow; it only rebuilds
firmware/core/font_3270.c.


